              "value": "Staggering Sail"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(incapacitation)\n\nWith a powerful lunge to the side, the spinosaurus uses its sail to slap the surface of the water, creating a crushing wave of water that deals 6d6 bludgeoning damage in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the water in the area must attempt a DC 30 Reflex save.\n\nCritical Success: The creature is unaffected.\nSuccess: The creature takes half damage.\nFailure: The creature takes full damage and is slowed 1 until the end of its next turn.\nCritical Failure: The creature takes double damage and is stunned 3."
